<title>USA: Harmony drops plan to acquire Unimedia.</title>
<headline>Harmony drops plan to acquire Unimedia.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harmony Holdings Inc said it has terminated its plans to acquire French company Unimedia SA after that company failed to respond completely to an initial draft agreement delivered by Harmony in July.</p>
<p>&quot;A preliminary agreement with Unimedia required the negotiation in good faith and execution before Sept. 30, 1996, of a definitive agreement,&quot; Harvey Bibicoff, chief executive officer, said in a statement.</p>
<p>Harmony said it received only partial comments to the initial draft on Sept. 24.</p>
</text>
